== offline: structural invariants ==
  ok   SPIRE HelmRelease present
  ok   spire-controller-manager enabled (renders ClusterSPIFFEID -> entries)
  ok   SPIRE OIDC Discovery Provider enabled (JWKS for OpenBao)
  ok   spiffe-csi-driver enabled (mounts agent socket into meshed pods)
  ok   trust domain is the one estate root (acme.internal), got 'acme.internal'
  ok   agent socket exposed for Envoy SDS (/run/spire/agent-sockets/spire-agent.sock)
  ok   istiod HelmRelease present
  ok   global.caName is absent (it's a no-op on Istio 1.24 and must not be reintroduced)
  ok   istiod's own CA server is NOT disabled — it must mint its own webhook serving cert (ENABLE_CA_SERVER: false was the ticket-04 bug: no CA bundle ever loads, webhook fails "tls: internal error")
  ok   meshConfig.trustDomain matches SPIRE's trust domain (acme.internal, not the cluster.local default)
  ok   sidecar injection mounts the SPIRE workload socket at Envoy's SDS default path (this, not caName, makes SPIRE the mesh CA)
  ok   spire injection template carries the spiffe.io/spire-managed-identity label block
  ok   mesh-wide PeerAuthentication STRICT
  ok   base ClusterSPIFFEID present
  ok   SVID template derives a spiffe:// path from pod/ns/sa
  ok   className set, so spire-controller-manager actually reconciles this object
  ok   AuthorizationPolicy present
  ok   authz admits by SPIFFE principal, not IP (['acme.internal/ns/mesh-demo/sa/ping'])
  ok   authz principal is scheme-less, not double-prefixed (['acme.internal/ns/mesh-demo/sa/ping'])
  ok   OpenBao HelmRelease present
  ok   OpenBao jwt-auth setup Job present
  ok   OpenBao jwt auth points at SPIRE's OIDC Discovery Provider JWKS
  ok   the discovery URL is https (the provider serves TLS on :8443; the Service publishes 443 only)
  ok   the discovery host is <svc>.spire-system -- the ONLY name in both the provider's `domains` list and its serving cert's DNS SANs
  ok   the SPIRE trust bundle is pinned as the CA (its cert chains to no public root)
  ok   the Job mounts the spire-bundle ConfigMap (which is why it runs in spire-system)
  ok   the package carries its own VERSION
  ok   the package carries OSCAL control claims (component-definition.json)
  ok   claims and bits carry the SAME version ('1.1.0') -- a package that versions its claims separately is two packages wearing one name
  ok   the package declares its membership (kustomization.yaml)
  ok   package membership includes namespaces.yaml
  ok   package membership includes spire/helmrelease.yaml
  ok   package membership includes spire/clusterspiffeid-mesh.yaml
  ok   package membership includes istio/helmrelease.yaml
  ok   package membership includes openbao/helmrelease.yaml
  ok   package membership includes openbao/jwt-auth.yaml
  ok   the ping->pong mTLS PROOF is not shipped as substrate
  ok   federation/ is not shipped wholesale -- each org applies its own file, not all four
  ok   SVID path is /posture/<version>/cage/<tier>/ns/<ns>/sa/<sa>
  ok   the tier segment reads the label cage-tier renders from the governed Namespace (one render, no second policy)
  ok   a pod with no tier label falls closed to `isolated`, never to an empty segment and never to baseline
  -- all offline invariants hold --
